Subject: startwizard: hide the KiCad update checkbox when KICAD_UPDATE_CHECK is off

Preferences hides its KiCad update checkbox in a build without the update
check; the start wizard's Updates & Privacy page does not, and its ticked box
does nothing. Hide it there too and word the intro for package updates only.

--- a/common/startwizard/startwizard_provider_privacy.cpp	2026-08-28 23:31:37.000000000 +0530
+++ b/common/startwizard/startwizard_provider_privacy.cpp	2026-11-09 14:25:13.229172134 +0530
@@ -36,6 +36,13 @@
             PANEL_STARTWIZARD_PRIVACY_BASE( aParent ),
             m_model( aModel )
     {
+#ifndef KICAD_UPDATE_CHECK
+        m_stIntro->SetLabel( _( "Allow connections to the Internet to check for updated versions of "
+                                "packages installed through the Plugin and Content Manager?" ) );
+        m_stIntro->Wrap( 550 );
+        m_cbAutoUpdateKiCad->Show( false );
+#endif
+
 #ifndef KICAD_USE_SENTRY
         m_sizerDataCollection->Show( false );
 #endif
